WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:12.430
If you were to walk up these stairs into that
building through a long hallway, you'd come

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:17.680
to the courtroom, where the Supreme Court
justices, dressed in their black robes, hear

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.510
their cases.

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:25.090
The Constitution establishes the judiciary
of which the Supreme Court is a part, as a

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:28.530
separate branch of the federal government.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:34.050
Under the Constitution, it's empowered to
hear all cases arising under the Constitution,

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:38.989
under the Laws of the United States, and Treaties.

00:00:38.989 --> 00:00:44.790
Alexander Hamilton called the judicial branch
the weakest branch of the federal government.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:52.370
He noted that Congress has the power of money,
the president has the power of the military,

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:55.650
and the courts have the power only of judgment.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:01:01.710
Meaning that the legitimacy of the courts
depends on the wisdom of their decisions.

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:07.450
Being the weakest branch does not mean, however,
that the Judiciary is a weak branch.

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.960
The Supreme Court is a very powerful institution.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:16.240
Some of its decisions have as much impact
as a major act of Congress or an important

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.150
decision of the president.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:25.070
Consider, for example, the Supreme Court's
decision in Citizens United in 2010.

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:31.130
In it, it declared that corporations and unions,
and by extension independent groups, can spend

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:35.329
unlimited amounts of money during election
campaigns.

00:01:35.329 --> 00:01:40.009
That decision has changed the way that we
elect our officials.

00:01:40.009 --> 00:01:45.740
In 2012, independent groups spent nearly a
billion dollars to try to influence the voters.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:52.859
In 2014, they spent so much money that the
number of televised political ads doubled

00:01:52.859 --> 00:01:55.509
from the previous midterm in 2010.

